#' Simulated shots
#'
#' A synthetic set of unblocked shot attempts between two fictional teams,
#' generated by `data-raw/shots.R` for examples and tests. Locations are
#' plausible but invented, and `xg` comes from a toy distance-and-angle model,
#' not a fitted one.
#'
#' All shots are taken towards the right-hand goal (the high-`x` end) of an
#' [IIHF] rink, in metres with the origin at the bottom-left corner of the
#' boards.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 1,500 rows and 8 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{shot_id}{Shot id.}
#'   \item{game_id}{Game id, 1-10.}
#'   \item{period}{Period, 1-3.}
#'   \item{team}{Shooting team, `"Lakeside"` or `"Northfield"`.}
#'   \item{x, y}{Shot location, in metres.}
#'   \item{xg}{Expected-goal probability from the toy model.}
#'   \item{goal}{`1` if the shot was a goal, else `0`.}
#' }
"shots"

utils::globalVariables(c("value", "count"))
